  <title class="- topic/title ">BIOS Requirement for NGU/NOC</title> 
  <body class="- topic/body "> 
    <p class="- topic/p ">BIOS is required to program UFI and CMI range register. There are mainly two categories of register programming. 
    </p> 
    <ol id="GUID-2B88C9EA-915F-4F2F-8E25-248C2F127BE5" class="- topic/ol "> 
      <li id="LI_050F2E1CA70642289CBF2093AE0DA2B1" class="- topic/li "> UFI security range register which includes two types of IMRs (covered under 
        <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-64B73CBF-EE16-4E49-8AEF-EB595AA49284.xml#GUID-64B73CBF-EE16-4E49-8AEF-EB595AA49284" class="- topic/xref "></xref> in detail) 
        <ol id="GUID-EDF389B0-F0C9-44DA-943B-5047F461DCD2" class="- topic/ol "> 
          <li id="LI_4A1B6B7C4B1549B0A9C587AD63E6B7D6" class="- topic/li ">IMR with power of two base and Mask 
          </li> 
          <li id="LI_81797EE159F149BB87A0309038DA691E" class="- topic/li ">IMR with 1 MB incremental space. 
          </li> 
        </ol> 
      </li> 
      <li id="LI_83A27D9C6B99457DB399AE36A4B56095" class="- topic/li "> CMI memory range registers for routing and specifying memory DIMM configuration 
      </li> 
    </ol> 
    <p class="- topic/p "> BIOS need to program the Memory population configuration for CCE and MC controller, for MC controller BIOS need to populate how Memory is distributed/shared b/w MC0 and MC1 on SOC and CCE range register need to be programmed with total Memory ( 0 to TOUUD). All these registers are exposed via MCHBAR range and BIOS need to configure them before MEM_CONFIG_DONE. Register details are captured in NGU HAS. 
    </p> 
    <p class="- topic/p "> Below Example shows CCE/MC ranges need to program for 24GB memory ( MC0 16GB , 8GB MC1) 
    </p> 
